From a9834b7179274f9376e99b9c1582de3ebd2a0de4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stel777 <274792865+Stel777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 19:51:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] feat(source-folders): dry-run preview + cross-path
 dedup before sync
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sync is now a reviewable reconcile instead of a silent apply:

- New read-only `plan()` + GET /api/brains/:id/sources/preview returns
  exactly what a sync WOULD do — to_add / to_update / to_remove /
  duplicates / unchanged — touching nothing.
- Cross-path dedup: a file whose exact content already exists in the brain
  under another path (e.g. a prior import) is flagged and skipped instead
  of duplicated. Best-effort (content hashed identically to ingest); files
  imported with different wrapping won't hash-match and show as add.
- The panel's "Sync now" runs the preview first and shows
  "add N · update K · remove M · skip D duplicates · U unchanged" with an
  Apply/Cancel confirm; nothing changes until Apply.
- SyncReport/response gain skipped_duplicates.

Verified on a throwaway brain: preview is read-only, node_modules stays
excluded, dedup skips an exact duplicate, update/unchanged classified
correctly; apply matched the preview.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
